--- /dev/null
+++ b/k8s/vault-agent-injector/aegis-vault-agent-annotations.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Vault Agent Injector annotations (token file at /vault/secrets/token)
+
+Attach these annotations to the *Pod template metadata* for your serving deployments (vLLM/Triton).
+
+These annotations assume:
+- Vault Agent Injector is installed in the cluster
+- Vault Kubernetes auth is configured
+- A Vault role exists that allows signing verification in Transit (verify endpoint)
+
+Example annotations:
+
+```yaml
+metadata:
+  annotations:
+    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject: "true"
+    vault.hashicorp.com/role: "REPLACE_ME_VAULT_ROLE"
+    # Write the Vault token to /vault/secrets/token so the initContainer can read it.
+    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-token: "true"
+    vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject-token-path: "/vault/secrets"
+```
+
+Notes:
+- The initContainer and main container will both see the injected volume at /vault/secrets.
+- Your code expects token file at:
+  - `/vault/secrets/token` (default)
+  - or env `VAULT_TOKEN_FILE` if you override it
